ntinues until all blocks are collected in the correct order\nOr maybe ACTION7 is a \"shoot\" action that shoots from the player's position, and the player needs to be in the right column to hit the green block.\nLet me test: move the player RIGHT to align with the green block (col ~50), then try ACTION7 to see if it collects the block.\nActually, wait. The player is at col 20-22 and the green block is at col 49-53. To align, I'd need to move RIGHT many times. Let me first check how many columns the player needs to move.\nPlayer center: ~col 21\nGreen block center: ~col 51\nDifference: 30 columns\nIf each RIGHT moves the player by 6 columns (like LEFT did), then I'd need 5 RIGHT actions to move 30 columns. But let me first check how much RIGHT moves the player.\nActually, let me just try: move RIGHT until near the green block, then use ACTION7.", "kind": "reasoning", "inContext": false}, {"label": "TOOL CALL: python", "content": "<tool_call>\n<function=python>\n<parameter=code>\n# Test: move RIGHT to align with green block, then try ACTION7\n# Player at col ~21, green block at col ~51\n# Let's try moving RIGHT several times\n\n# First, let's see how much RIGHT moves the player\nresult = action(['RIGHT'])\nseg = current_frame.segmentation\nfor n in seg['nodes']:\n    if n['color'] == 'b':\n        cols = [p[1] for p in n['boundary']]\n        print(f\"After 1 RIGHT: player col {min(cols)}-{max(cols)}\")\n        break\n\n# Move more RIGHT to reach col ~50\nresult = action(['RIGHT', 'RIGHT', 'RIGHT', 'RIGHT', 'RIGHT'])\nseg = current_frame.segmentation\nfor n in seg['nodes']:\n    if n['color'] == 'b':\n        cols = [p[1] for p in n['boundary']]\n        print(f\"After 5 more RIGHT: player col {min(cols)}-{max(cols)}\")\n        break\n\n# Check if green block still exists\ngreen_count = sum(1 for n in seg['nodes'] if n['color'] == 'N')\nprint(f\"Green blocks: {green_count}\")\n</parameter>\n</function>\n</tool_call>", "kind": "tool", "inContext": true}, {"label": "T